Description: Universal archive extractor for GNU/Linux
 Karchiver is a simple and safe command-line tool that extracts
 archives using the system's native tools (tar, unzip, 7z, ar, ...).
 It runs each extractor via execvp without a shell, extracts into a
 staging directory first, verifies paths and symlinks, and enforces
 a maximum size limit to defend against path traversal and zip bombs.
 .
 It integrates with desktop environments through a .desktop file
 and MIME type associations, providing "Extract Here" and
 "Extract To..." actions in file managers.
 .
 Supported formats: tar, tar.gz, tar.bz2, tar.xz, tar.zst, gz, bz2,
 xz, zst, lzma, z, zip, jar, war, apk, 7z, rar, lha, lzh, cab, deb, ar.
